00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,900
-的确有点迷恋我 -是啊
- back in high school. ?- Yeah.

182
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,050
看来他只喜欢咱们这类型的
I guess he's got a type.

183
00:06:37,050 --> 00:06:38,620
别闹了 别闹了
Stop it! Stop it.

184
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:40,800
-我哪能和你比 -如果你不介意的话
- I am nothing like -- - Well, if you don't mind, actually,

185
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,600
我想先进门
I'd like to come in?

186
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:43,180
我得去马厩看看状况
I got to see man about a horse.

187
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,317
可我们这没有...
But we don't have --

188
00:06:45,317 --> 00:06:46,560
那是种婉转的说法
That's a classy way of saying

189
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,740
是我要去释放一下膀胱的意思
I got to make my bladder gladder.

190
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:48,870
卫生间 好的
Bathroom! Uh, yes...

191
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:50,840
在走廊尽头 右手边
Uh, end of the hall on -- on the right. Yep.

192
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:53,260
那些青少年时尚杂志是我们女儿的
Oh, and the Teen Vogues are our daughter's!

193
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,040
我们根本不知道黛米·洛瓦托是谁
We don't even know who Demi Lovato is!

194
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,980
好吧 拉里怎么又跑出去了
Okay, how did Larry get out again?

195
00:06:57,980 --> 00:06:59,393
天啊 肯定是你姐
God, it must've been your sister.

196
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,900
你猜谁在卫生间里
So, guess who is in the bathroom.

197
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,780
我的惊喜不过是蜡烛而已
Oh, well, my surprise was just candles,

198
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:04,597
但我也来者不拒
but I'm not saying no.

199
00:07:04,597 --> 00:07:06,700
不 是博
No, uh... It's Bo.

200
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:07,756
-我的博 -不
- My Bo? - No --

201
00:07:07,756 --> 00:07:09,740
应该说是帕姆的博
Well, technically, he's-he's more Pam's Bo,

202
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,980
而我是你的米奇尔
and I am your Mitchell.

203
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:13,660
但是的 他来接帕姆和宝宝回家
But yes. Yeah, he's here to take Pam and the baby home!

204
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,420
这是多好的事啊
I mean, how great is that?

205
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:16,840
卡梅隆·塔克
Cameron Tucker!

206
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,740
从我家里滚出去
Get the hell out of my house.

207
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:19,900
合上你的双臂
Close those arms.

208
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,200
别这样 小卡
Come on, Cam.

209
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,340
-是啊 别这样 小卡 -不
- Yeah, come on, Cam. - No.

210
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:26,220
我不准你接近我姐姐
You are not getting anywhere near my sister.

211
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,080
快滚
Now get out!

212
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,720
快点 快滚
Let's go! Get out!

213
00:07:30,805 --> 00:07:33,022
那他就会改成在门口等帕姆啊
Uh, won't he just wait for Pam outside?

214
00:07:33,022 --> 00:07:34,841
-因为 -好吧 给我回来
- I mean -- - Okay, you know... Come back in!

215
00:07:35,573 --> 00:07:36,660
太好了 拉里又跑出去了
Great. There goes Larry again.

216
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:39,460
我开始认为它不愿意在咱家待着了
You know, I'm starting to think he's unhappy living here.

217
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:43,860
很好 很好
Good. Good.

218
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,960
有魔术贴的鞋不行
Uh, no Velcro.

219
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:48,060
我们的品牌要更高级些
Our brand is a little more upscale.

220
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:53,740
又一个买家看同一双脚看腻了
Another buyer is tired of seeing the same feet.

221
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,320
这成了我的错吗
Oh, it's my fault now?

222
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,660
他也没为保持新鲜感做出什么贡献啊
What's he doing to keep things interesting?

223
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,920
我为什么在乎
Why do I care?

224
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,920
真没想到你愿意这么做
I'm surprised you were open to this.

225
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,500
真没想到你这么熟练
I'm surprised you know how to do this.

226
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:04,700
别忘了
Don't forget,

227
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,880
我们一会得去老妈公司把鞋发出去
we have to get over to mom's work to ship shoes later.

228
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,800
等一下 你一直在用老妈的快递吗
Wait a second, you're using Mom's FedEx?

229
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,220
每次她和老爸晚上出去奢侈
Every time she and Dad have a fancy night out,

230
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,460
她总会用"卢克的大学基金"
she uses the hashtag "Luke's college fund."

231
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,140
所以我也占占她的便宜
So, yeah, I'm using her account.

232
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:20,620
你是不是有瞒着一些关于这房子的事
Is there something you're not telling me about this house?

233
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,760
我有点感觉到了凶杀案的气息
I am kind of getting a murdery vibe.

234
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,920
唯一与这幢房子有关的"杀"
The only killing that's ever gonna happen in this house

235
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,960
是你哪天转卖时 会杀光买家的钱包
is the one that's gonna happen when you sell the place.

236
00:08:27,581 --> 00:08:30,160
笑声会激怒鬼魂们 菲尔
Laughter makes the spirits hungry, Phil!

237
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:30,856
鬼魂们
Spirits?

238
00:08:30,856 --> 00:08:32,604
有不止一个的意思吗
You means there's more than one?

239
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,020
吉尔
Hi, Gil.

240
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,200
等等 不 吉尔
Wait. No. Gil?

241
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,420
歌洛
Hey, Glo?

242
00:08:39,723 --> 00:08:41,641
你能来我真的很高兴
Uh, super stoked you're here.

243
00:08:41,883 --> 00:08:44,000
希望你能听我一个小建议
If-if I could give you one tiny note?

244
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:44,980
格拉哈姆太太的害怕等级
Mrs. Graham's terror level,

245
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:45,860
我们需要把它往下降
which should be going down,

246
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,720
-但目前在升高 -我的也在升高
- is actually going up. - Mine too.

247
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:49,780
事实上我已经慌了
Actually, I'm panicking right now!

248
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,360
你不会相信我现在所感受到的
You can't believe what I'm sensing right now!

249
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:56,340
这里有嗡嗡声 震动 恐惧
There is like, a humming sound, vibrations, fear!

250
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:57,680
我很肯定那都是我发出来的
I'm pretty sure that's all coming off of me,

251
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:59,638
因为我很需要的这桩生意要黄了
because I'm about to lose a sale I really need.

252
00:08:59,638 --> 00:09:02,180
这样如何 你稍微包装一下
How about this? Just-just spin it a little.

253
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,480
你想让我做什么
What are you asking me to do?

254
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:05,461
在房地产界 没有烂房
In real estate, there are no dumps.

255
00:09:05,461 --> 00:09:07,200
只有待修房
There are fixer-uppers.

256
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,800
面积小就说很温馨
A small house is cozy.

257
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:10,340
我们又不知道这个灵体是坏的
How do we know this presence is bad?

258
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,220
比如《鬼马小精灵》或圣灵
What about Casper? Or the Holy Ghost?

259
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,080
人们特喜欢那种的
People love those guys --

260
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:13,380
菲尔
Phil.

261
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,717
情况很糟 是不是
It's bad, isn't it?

262
00:09:15,717 --> 00:09:18,098
不 情况其实很好
No, it's-it's actually really good.

263
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,080
歌洛莉亚正告诉我她有了很大进展
Gloria was just saying she's making real progress.

264
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,274
-对吧 歌洛莉亚 -抱歉
- Right, Gloria? - I'm sorry,

265
00:09:21,274 --> 00:09:23,560
这幢房子里有很令人不安的灵体
but there is a disturbing presence in this house

266
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,340
我觉得我也驱逐不了
that I don't think that I can drive out.

267
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,140
那我肯定不买了
Well, that is it for me.

268
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:28,740
菲尔 如果你有不闹鬼
Phil, please let me know

269
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:30,240
而且也离我的灵媒很近的房子
if you find something less haunted,

270
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,220
请你一定要告诉我
still within walking distance to my psychic.

271
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:35,800
我们马上回来
We'll be right back.

272
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:36,740
博 你想喝冰茶吗
Bo, you want some iced tea?

273
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,260
那太好了 谢谢
That'd be great. Thank you.

274
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:39,740
不 不准给他冰茶喝
No, you are not giving him iced tea.

275
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,060
这可不是花园派对
This is not a garden party.

276
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,320
但他大老远来弥补错误
But he did come all this way to make things right.

277
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,220
你知道吗 小卡
And you know what, Cam?

278
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,639
监狱是会改变人的
Prison changes people.

279
00:09:45,639 --> 00:09:47,060
-是吗 -总是往好了改
- Oh, does it? - Always in a good

280
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,260
永久性的改变
and permanent way.

281
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,640
看看他啊
I mean, look at him...

282
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:51,340
不 不要看他
No. Do not look at him.

283
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,420
他就是个男妖
He is a siren.

284
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:55,100
他用那双美丽的大蓝眼勾引你
He draws you in with those big beautiful blue eyes,

285
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,399
等你反应过来 你已经
and the next thing you know, you're giving him

286
00:09:56,399 --> 00:09:58,140
把你曾祖父内战时期的刺刀给他了
your great-grandfather's Civil War bayonet

287
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,640
而他拿去卖了买魔豆
and he's selling it for Magic Beans.

288
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,860
魔豆是他喝的威士忌牌子
It's the brand of whiskey he drinks.

289
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:04,940
我认为该给他第二次机会
I just -- I think he deserves a second chance.

290
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,540
你为什么突然在意起
Why do you suddenly care so much

291
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:07,616
帕姆和博能不能复合
if Pam and Bo are back together?

292
00:10:07,616 --> 00:10:09,420
我是个离婚律师 小卡
I'm a divorce lawyer, Cam.

293
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,620
我总能看到家庭四分五裂
I see families torn apart all the time.

294
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:14,040
人的感情那么受伤代价太高了
The emotional cost is just too high.

295
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:16,880
一切的代价都太高太贵了
The cost of everything is too high!

296
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,340
帕姆自己铺了床
Look, Pam made her bed.

297
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:20,100
现在需要她从床上下来
Now she needs to get out of it

298
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,480
我才能把床垫翻一下接着赚钱
so I can flip the mattress to make some money off of it.

299
00:10:22,837 --> 00:10:25,116
我没想到听起来会这么像皮条客
Sounded more pimpy than I intended.

300
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,880
或许帕姆不想在楼上住下去了
Maybe Pam doesn't want to live upstairs anymore.

301
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:30,940
或许她想跟他回密苏里
Maybe she wants to go with him to Missouri.

302
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:33,740
又或许是你不想让帕姆在楼上住下去了
Or maybe you don't want Pam to live upstairs

303
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:35,240
是你想让她跟他回密苏里
and you want her to go home to Missouri.

304
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,580
我不小心听到你们说话
I couldn't help but overhear,

305
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:37,980
因为我们就在同一间房间里
since we're practically in the same room

306
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:39,220
你们说话又很大声
and you ain't exactly whispering...

307
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,880
我能替自己说几句话吗
Can I say something on my behalf?

308
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:41,920
不 不能
No, you may not!

309
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:43,220
因为如果你在乎我姐姐
Because if you cared about my sister,

310
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:45,420
小卡尔霍恩出生时你就会在这
you would've been here the moment baby Calhoun was born!

311
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,940
我知道 但在我因为
I know, but when I got out of jail

312
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,080
打了警马服刑出狱后
for punching that police horse,

313
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,820
我发现我的卡车被拖走了
I discovered my truck had been towed.

314
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,815
我不得不卖血浆换现金
I had to sell my plasma for cash.

315
00:10:51,815 --> 00:10:54,120
他会替别人着想 多高尚
He thinks of others. Very noble.

316
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,340
我只听到了没车又没钱
All I'm hearing is no car, no money,

317
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,600
免疫系统低下
compromised immune system.

318
00:10:57,820 --> 00:10:58,840
这模样真值得我们学习
What a great role model.

319
00:10:58,960 --> 00:10:59,920
是的 他模样的确不错
And yes, he could be a model,

320
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,953
但我是不会被那对美丽的蓝眼睛蛊惑的
but I will not be distracted by those beautiful big blue eyes.

321
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:05,040
小卡 我都懂
Cam, I get it, all right?

322
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,520
我犯过很多错
I made a lot of mistakes.

323
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,679
但就像我的血液一样
But like my plasma,

324
00:11:07,679 --> 00:11:10,674
我要贯彻积极的B型阳性
I decided to "B-positive."

325
00:11:10,705 --> 00:11:12,580
我搭车 我打奇怪的零工
I hitchhiked, I took odd jobs,

326
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:14,040
为了到这来能做的我都做了
whatever I could do to get here.

327
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,300
帕姆 我们的孩子卡尔霍恩
I mean, Pam, our boy Calhoun,

328
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,340
他们是我的家人
they're my family.

329
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,360
你也是我的家人
Hell, you're my family.

330
00:11:21,288 --> 00:11:22,426
我很想相信你 博
Okay, I want to believe you, Bo,

331
00:11:22,426 --> 00:11:23,554
但我...
but, yeah, I just --

332
00:11:23,664 --> 00:11:25,520
我被伤过太多次了
yeah, I've been burned too many times.

333
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:27,360
说到伤 我有样东西想给你看看
About that... I got something to show you.

334
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,253
塔克 石墙杰克逊将军
Old Stonewall Tucker

335
00:11:34,253 --> 00:11:36,180
会希望这东西能物归原主的
would've wanted you to have this back.

336
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:36,800
石墙将军
Stonewall.

337
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,798
希望不是从人家雕像手里偷的
I'm guessing his statue's no longer in the park.

338
00:11:38,798 --> 00:11:41,480
-你不是卖了吗 -那是过去的博
- I thought you sold this. - Welp, that was the old Bo.

339
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,911
全新的博攒钱买回来还给你
The new Bo saved up and bought it back for you.

340
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,380
-你瞧 -相信我
- See? - Believe me,

341
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,880
我只想弥补过错
I'm trying to do the right thing.

342
00:11:50,219 --> 00:11:51,200
博
Bo...

343
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,800
他怎么会在这
What the hell is he doing here?!

344
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,869
帕梅隆
Now, Pameron,

345
00:11:54,869 --> 00:11:56,876
博是来重新争取你和小卡尔霍恩的
Bo came back for you and baby Calhoun!

346
00:11:56,876 --> 00:11:58,600
是的 给他个机会好吗
Yeah, just-just give him a chance, okay?

347
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,780
我的天
Oh, my gosh.

348
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:00,818
就是他吗
Is this him?

349
00:12:00,818 --> 00:12:02,160
那是我儿子吗
Is-is that my boy?

350
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:04,800
不 这是我的车 我有个迷你小司机
No. This is my car and I have a little tiny driver.

351
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:05,820
当然是他
Of course it's him!

352
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,264
你别靠近我们
You stay away from us,

353
00:12:07,264 --> 00:12:08,820
-博勒加德·拉维恩·约翰逊 -拜托
- Beauregard Lavern Johnson! - Come on --

354
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:11,820
也别再用你致命的蓝眼睛视奸我
And stop undressing me with your devil blue eyes!

355
00:12:11,868 --> 00:12:13,000
这样吧 我去
Okay, You know what? I'll-I'll go --

356
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,620
我去和她谈谈
I'll go talk to her.

357
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:20,060
谢谢你刚才在小卡面前维护我
Hey, thank you for pleading my case back there with Cam.

358
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:22,300
我看得出来你是个好律师
I can tell, you're good lawyer.

359
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,216
我也看得出来你是个好人
And I can tell you are a good man.

360
00:12:24,216 --> 00:12:25,940
我会一直支持你的
I am team Bo all the way.

361
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:26,760
那太好了
All right, good.

362
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,790
因为我可能需要一些法律建议
'Cause I-I might need some legal counsel.

363
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,860
那个刺刀不是我买回来的
See, I-I didn't buy that bayonet back,

364
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,020
是我偷回来的
so much as I stole it.

365
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:32,800
天啊
Oh, dear.

366
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,780
大家 打扰一下
Excuse me, everyone!

367
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:39,580
作为创始人
As founder of this company,

368
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:42,100
我用血泪独自创立了这间公司
which I built with my own sweat and tears,

369
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,500
我想简单说几句
I'd like to say a few words.

370
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,980
在迈进未来前
Before going into the future,

371
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,740
向我们的过去致敬是很重要的
it's important we honor how we got here.

372
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:48,440
所以我做了个小短片
So I put together a little presentation.

373
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,400
爸 我们在吃冰激凌
Dad, we're having ice cream.

374
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,460
他们可以边舔边看
They can lick and watch.

375
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,820
马尾男 关灯
Ponytail, lights.

376
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:03,100
一幅横贯欧洲的铁幕正在落下
An iron curtain was descending over Europe.

377
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:05,940
但在俄亥俄州的杨斯顿市 一个孩子诞生了
But in Youngstown, Ohio, a child is born.

378
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:09,540
虽然少年时期的杰·普里契特是个明星球员
While young Jay Pritchett was superstar athlete,

379
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,340
但他还是个艺术家
he was also an artist

380
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:13,540
梦想要为某个业界带来革命性变化
who dreamed of revolutionizing an industry --

381
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:15,400
衣柜业
closets.

382
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,320
他就是不能让我当一天主角
He just couldn't let me have my day.

383
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,300
非得喧宾夺主
He had to make it all about him.

384
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:20,400
真是太恶心了
It was disgusting.

385
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:21,820
不过...
Although...

386
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:23,940
他扮演自己父亲
the scene of him playing his father

387
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,640
拒绝借他创业资金的那一幕
denying him a startup loan?

388
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,760
出人意料地动人心弦
Surprisingly powerful.

389
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:30,000
当全美忙着跳哈娑舞时
While America was doing the Hustle,

390
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,500
杰也在"舞"力全开要建起商业帝国
Jay as hustling to build an empire,

391
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,720
这就是为什么有家报纸称他为
which is why one newspaper called him

392
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,780
"柜界最努力之人"
"The hardest working man in closets."

393
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,400
那是他自己打的广告
That was an ad.

394
00:13:38,741 --> 00:13:40,360
谁能料想到这家
Who would've thought the company,

395
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:41,920
由那个男孩建起的公司
built by that little boy,

396
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,580
有一天也能在
would one day be the toast

397
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:45,780
国际衣柜界里成为业界楷模
of the international closet world?

398
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,520
恭喜大家 我们做到了
Congratulations. We did it.

399
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,500
玛格丽特调了一些酒
Margaret's mixing some drinks.

400
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,800
下午愉快
Enjoy the afternoon.

401
00:13:55,862 --> 00:13:57,608
-赞啊 -谢谢
-Nice! -Thank you.

402
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,740
格拉哈姆太太马上要走了
Okay, Mrs. Graham's car is on its way!

403
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,180
你只剩五分钟时间说服她
You have five minutes to convince her

404
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:06,139
这房子没问题
that this house is fine!

405
00:14:06,139 --> 00:14:07,280
有东西在这墙里 菲尔
Something's in this wall, Phil.

406
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:09,420
不 我已经听够这些鬼话了
No, I am done with this nonsense!

407
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,680
真不敢相信这话居然
I can't believe I'm hearing this

408
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,240
出自一个相信魔术[法]的人之口
from a person that believes in magic!

409
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,660
以后我不会承认我说过这话
I'm not the one who told you this,

410
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,760
但魔术不是魔法
but magic isn't actually magic.

411
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,500
这不是真从你耳里拿出来的
That didn't come from your ear.

412
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,960
什么 怎么可能
What? How?

413
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:22,020
你也是他们的一员
You're with them.

414
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,840
哪有什么"他们"啊 歌洛莉亚
There is no "them," Gloria.

415
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:26,320
所有人对这个戏法都会说"什么 怎么可能"
Everybody says "What? How?" to that trick.

416
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,360
这就是魔术的原理
That's how magic works.

417
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:28,520
一些看起来超自然的事情
Things that seem supernatural

418
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:30,240
其实都有非常合理的解释
actually have a perfectly logical explanation.

419
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:32,140
这面墙是热的 菲尔
This wall is warm, Phil.

420
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,940
正在散发出邪能
It's radiating evil.

421
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,580
才没有散发出什么邪...
It is not radiating evil --

422
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,600
的确是热的耶
Oh, that is warm.

423
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:38,900
这又是怎么回事
What was that?

424
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,520
-电路不行吗 菲尔 -你好大胆子
- Faulty wiring, Phil?! - How dare you.

425
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,460
我才不会卖别人电路不行的房子呢
I would never sell a house with faulty wiring!

426
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,399
你也能听到对吧
You can hear that, right?

427
00:14:46,399 --> 00:14:48,452
你惹他们生气了
You made them angry.

428
00:14:48,452 --> 00:14:49,898
我才不信这一套
I don't believe in any of this!

429
00:14:50,376 --> 00:14:51,434
以防万一...
But just in case...

430
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,120
-这是什么 圣水吗 -不是
- What is this? Holy water? - ?No.

431
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,238
黄瓜水
Cucumber water.

432
00:14:55,238 --> 00:14:57,418
你以为我这好皮肤是凭空来的吗
You think this skin just happens?

433
00:14:57,535 --> 00:14:59,343
好... 好吧
Okay...okay.

434
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:00,620
卖家很快要回家了
The sellers are on their way home.

435
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:02,090
我们就把东西物归原位
Let's just put everything back the way we found it

436
00:15:02,090 --> 00:15:02,829
然后顺路去个教堂吧
and maybe swing by a church.

437
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:05,100
挂上啊
Come on!

438
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:09,358
天啊
Oh, my God!

439
00:15:09,358 --> 00:15:10,206
有蜜蜂
Bees! ?

440
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:13,039
快跑快跑快跑啊
Oh! Go! Go, go, go, go, go, go!

441
00:15:13,039 --> 00:15:15,860
好消息 格拉哈姆太太 原来只是蜜蜂
Good news, Mrs. Graham, it's only bees!

442
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,700
我会再跟进公证行的文件
I'll follow up with the escrow documents!

443
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:18,900
恭喜你了
Congrats! Ow!

444
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:23,860
很有意思的小电影啊 老爸
So, that was a fun movie, Dad.

445
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:26,117
虽然有一点喧宾夺主了
Kind of made it all about you, though.

446
00:15:26,117 --> 00:15:28,300
瞎说 来一杯杰丁尼
Nonsense. Try a Jay-tini.

447
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,320
不用了
I'm good.

448
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,348
恭喜参展 老板
Congratulations on the Expo, boss.

449
00:15:31,348 --> 00:15:31,860
-谢谢 -谢谢
- Thanks. - Thanks.

450
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,640
我觉得那不知道啥名的女人是在对我说
I think that what's her name was talking to me.

451
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:35,460
是吗
Oh?

452
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,380
玛格丽特 我的孩子来这里做什么
Oh, Margaret, what are my kids doing here?

453
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,040
这些孩子来用我们公司的货运
Oh, the kids have been using the company shipping.

454
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:42,800
已经好几周了
They've been coming in for weeks.

455
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,580
我好醉啊
I am so drunk.

456
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:45,940
我是不是在大声吼
Am I screaming?

457
00:15:50,022 --> 00:15:51,582
你们俩个在搞什么鬼
What do you two think you're doing?

458
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,540
我们俩就是来恭喜你们
We just came to congratulate you

459
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,620
刚发生的那件事
on that thing that happened.

460
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,200
-再给你们一次机会 -好吧
- Try again. - Fine.

461
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,820
但这件事怎么说都有点怪
But there's no nice way to say this.

462
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:58,880
我开始了一家公司
I started a company

463
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,940
专门把艾丽克斯那些恶心臭烘烘的原味鞋
selling Alex's disgusting, smelly shoes

464
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:01,640
卖给恋足变态们
to feet freaks.

465
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:03,320
这也太恶心了吧
Wow, that is so gross!

466
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,340
是很有胆识
More like gutsy.

467
00:16:04,561 --> 00:16:05,940
要想白手起家一家公司
You got to get your hands dirty

468
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,520
就要能不怕苦不怕累不怕脏
to build a company from the ground up.

469
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:08,780
我为你感到骄傲 卢克
I'm proud of you, Luke.

470
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,179
等等
Uh, hold on.

471
00:16:10,179 --> 00:16:12,620
是我想到去旧货店买鞋
It was my idea to start buying thrift-store shoes.

472
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:14,560
我扩大业务 还让利润加倍
I expanded the business and doubled our profits.

473
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,780
你看到艾丽克斯做的了吗
You see what Alex did?

474
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,680
她让业务增长
She grew the business.

475
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:18,880
把生意带到了更高的境界
She took it to the next level.

476
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:21,940
她做到了卢克尝试了许多年
She was able to achieve what Luke couldn't

477
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,300
但一直都做不到的事
despite years of trying.

478
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:24,140
其实也才几...
It's really only been a few --

479
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:25,900
没有根 你怎么成长
You can't grow what doesn't exist!

480
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,200
他们是在吵他们的事情了
Okay. Well, they're on their thing now.

481
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:27,640
我们赶紧走人
Just walk away.

482
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,400
你知道我陪伴了这公司多久吗
Do you know how long I've been with this company?

483
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,600
美国换了7任总统
Seven presidents.

484
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:33,700
还有4任教皇 是的 我看了你那电影
And four popes. Yes, Dad, I saw the movie.

485
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:35,820
你就不能让我今天威风一天吗
Couldn't you just let me have today?

486
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:37,840
-你为什么没打给我 -你说什么呢
- Why didn't you call me? - What are you talking about?

487
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,620
今天早上 当你听到这大消息时
This morning. When you got the big news.

488
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:41,220
我现在已经不是这公司的一部分了吗
I mean, am I not a part of this anymore?

489
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,180
现在是这情况了吗
Is that what's going on here?

490
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,200
我没打给你
I didn't call you

491
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,180
是因为我在等着你打给我祝贺我
because I was waiting for you to call me and say,

492
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:47,700
"恭喜啊 你成功了 乖女儿"
"Congratulations, you did it, honey."

493
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,409
结果我却得来这里
Instead, I had to come here

494
00:16:49,409 --> 00:16:50,800
看一部"杰拉伯的劳伦斯"
and watch "Lawrence of A-Jay-bia."

495
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,221
-不然大家怎么会记得我的存在 -什么
- How else would anybody know I even existed? - What?

496
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:55,880
我整个职业生涯都在努力打进那展览会
I spent my entire career trying to get in the Expo,

497
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,620
你接掌公司两年内就做到了
and you come in and get it done in 2 years.

498
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,100
别这样 不用说也知道
Come on, it goes without saying

499
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:02,560
这间公司是因为有你才有今天
that this company would be nothing without you.

500
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:03,120
不 不知道
No, it doesn't.

501
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:05,380
-我就要听到你说出来 -你认真的吗
- Let me hear you say it. - Seriously?

502
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:06,680
是的 我要听
Yes. I want to hear it.

503
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,800
爸 如果不是你
Dad, if it weren't for you,

504
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,980
我们也不会有今天的成就
we wouldn't be where we are today.

505
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,820
您所有的辛勤付出
All of your hard work

506
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:17,820
为我们今日的成功打下了夯实的基础
laid the foundation for our success.

507
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:20,460
换你了
Now you.

508
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:22,760
如果我这么说 会显得太自大
Well, if I say it, it'll sound a little conceited.

509
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:25,380
不是让你说自己 是说我
No, not about you! About me!

510
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:27,940
你...
It's...

511
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:29,540
达成了这令人难以置信的成就
an unbelievable accomplishment.

512
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,720
你大大地超过我的期望
You've exceeded all my expectations,

513
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,540
而我的期望本来已经设得非常高了
which were ridiculously high to begin with.

514
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:36,360
公司找不到比你更好的接班人了
The company could not be in better hands.

515
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:39,817
谢谢你 爸爸
Thanks, Dad.

516
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:43,220
好吧 我们就先假设
Okay, let's just agree

517
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:44,820
你的出发点是好的
that your heart was in the right place

518
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:46,360
就是你还小卡刺刀这件事
giving Cam back his bayonet.

519
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,100
但像你这样的体面人...
But knowing what a decent person you are,

520
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:50,007
我确定你一定有计划要...
I'm sure you're planning on --

521
00:17:50,007 --> 00:17:51,685
博 开门
Bo, open this door!

522
00:17:52,709 --> 00:17:53,675
博
Bo!

523
00:17:54,347 --> 00:17:55,020
博
Bo --

524
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:57,100
你是打算让我在车里等你多久啊
How long you expect me to wait out there in the car?

525
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,160
天啊 求你告诉我她是你的出租车司机
Oh, God, please tell me this is your cab driver.

526
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:00,220
我叫海瑟
I'm Heather.

527
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,960
就像海色 不过我是"瑟"
It's like feather, but with an "H".

528
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,280
我认识你这名字
I'm familiar with the name.

529
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,440
亲爱的 我很快就出来
Uh, I'll be right out, sweetie.

530
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,960
先等我跟客户聊完就行
I'm just finishing up with my client.

531
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,540
好的 品克先生 您就等着
Okay, Mr. Pringle, you can expect delivery

532
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,541
一公与一母南美栗鼠送到您府上
of one male and one female chinchilla

533
00:18:11,541 --> 00:18:12,668
只需等...
in the next...

534
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:14,396
好险 她走了
Phew. Good. She's gone.

535
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:17,300
你能相信我是随机应变 现场编的吗
Can you believe I just thought of that on the spot?

536
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,640
我不要下楼 小卡
I'm not going down there, Cam.

537
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,580
我一到他身边就不清醒
I don't trust myself around him.

538
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:24,500
我看到他的脸庞 他的声音
I see that face, I hear that voice,

539
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,280
我的心就融化
I go all gooey.

540
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:27,080
这话你的同性恋友人十分赞同
You're preaching to the gay man's choir, here.

541
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,620
但你得为自己做决定
But you have to decide for yourself,

542
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:30,360
而且你得保持清醒
and you need to keep a clear head.

543
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:31,320
要不这样吧
You know what? All right.

544
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,820
教你一招我当年
So, here's a trick that I used

545
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,520
青春期情窦初开时用的招数
when I was coming of age.

546
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:36,880
我当时有一点缺乏自制力
So, I had a little bit of a self-control problem,

547
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:38,880
我会在我的手腕上绑一个橡皮筋
and I would put a rubber band around my wrist

548
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,360
每当我有冲动想要...
and flick it every time I got the urge

549
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,373
我就会弹一下
to...flick it.

550
00:18:43,405 --> 00:18:44,952
以前我们一起看有型男的电视剧
You used to snap one of those like crazy

551
00:18:44,952 --> 00:18:46,440
《正义前锋》时 你总疯狂弹啊
whenever we watched "Dukes of Hazzard."

552
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:48,600
是啊 所以我平安看完7季
Yeah. I got through all seven seasons --

553
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:49,740
一次特殊"事故"都没发生
zero incidents.

554
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:52,480
好了
Okay.

555
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:53,980
想说什么说吧
Say your piece.

556
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:54,920
但我先告诉你
But I'll tell you right now,

557
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,400
我可不会轻易被你说服
I ain't gonna make it easy for you.

558
00:18:57,045 --> 00:18:59,803
你看起来真美啊 小帕姆
You sure look pretty, Pam'n'cheese.

559
00:19:01,816 --> 00:19:03,107
博
Oh, Bo...

560
00:19:03,801 --> 00:19:04,863
过来抱抱
Come here.

561
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:07,680
我们促成了这一对
We did that.

562
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:09,160
是啊 是我们促成的
Yeah. Yeah, we did.

563
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,880
我知道我配不上你
I know I don't deserve you,

564
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,740
但如果你与卡尔愿意要我
but if you and Cal will have me,

565
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:15,440
我发誓我愿意用我的余生
I promise to spend every day of my life

566
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,900
向你证明我值得托付
proving that I am worthy.

567
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,860
我的天啊
Oh, my God!

568
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:20,720
看看这戒指真是太美了
Look at this beautiful ring!

569
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,080
简直太完美...
It's just so perfect --

570
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,620
谁是海瑟
Who's Heather?

571
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,060
这是卖我戒指的珠宝商的名字
Oh, that's the name of the jeweler I bought it from.

572
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:30,618
海瑟戒指与其他东西店
Heather's Rings and... things.

573
00:19:30,618 --> 00:19:32,367
够了 不行 不可以
Okay! Nope! Mnh-mnh! Nope!

574
00:19:32,367 --> 00:19:34,400
不行 连我都没办法再为你开脱了
No, even I can't spin this anymore.

575
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:36,061
听我说 博就是个烂人
All right. Bo is a disaster, okay?

576
00:19:36,061 --> 00:19:37,740
他一点都没变
He -- he hasn't changed one bit.

577
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,263
他就是个骗子 还是个贼
He is a liar, he is a thief,

578
00:19:39,263 --> 00:19:40,579
他白天就开始喝酒 他...
he is a day drinker, he --

579
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,300
他从海瑟那里偷来的这戒指
He stole that ring from Heather,

580
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:44,480
而海瑟人正在外面 以防你拒绝了博
who's waiting outside for him in case you say no.

581
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,389
你怎么能说出这些话
Hey! You can't say any of that!

582
00:19:46,389 --> 00:19:48,820
我们有律师客户保密权
That's attorney-client privilege!

583
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:49,860
他还是个傻逼
He's also an idiot.

584
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,940
来 我才不会让你跟卡尔
Look, okay, I am not letting you and Cal

585
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,500
接近这烂人一步呢 好吗
go anywhere near him, all right?

586
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:55,400
真不敢相信我居然
I cannot believe I got drawn in

587
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,000
又被你大而深邃的蓝眼珠给迷惑了
by those big beautiful blue eyes again.

588
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:58,360
滚出我家
Get out of my house.

589
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,900
这你说了不算吧 是吧
Well, it's not really up to you, now is it?

590
00:20:01,638 --> 00:20:03,786
你觉得呢 帕姆美人
What you think, Pamburger?

591
00:20:05,078 --> 00:20:06,197
我...
Well, I --

592
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,880
滚出去
Get the hell out!

593
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:13,460
行
Fine.

594
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:17,840
还好我有善待海瑟 为她留着空调
I'm glad I left the air conditioning on for Heather.

595
00:20:22,647 --> 00:20:23,348
我还...
I even got --

596
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:25,380
谢谢你了 米奇尔
Thanks, Mitchell...

597
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:26,780
谢谢你那样为我着想
...for taking care of me like that.

598
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,960
你在这里也有个家
You have a home here

599
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:31,440
-你在这里待多久都行 -米奇尔
- as long as you need it, okay? - Aww, Mitchell,

600
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:33,280
你真的有在为她着想
you really are looking out for my sister.

601
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,000
听我说 帕姆
And you know what, Pam?

602
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:35,960
既然你还会在这里多住一段时间
As long as you're gonna be staying here for a little while,

603
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:37,220
你要多注意随手关门啊
you got to mind the door a little better.

604
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,360
拉里老是会溜出去
Larry keeps getting out.

605
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:40,980
-你再说一次"拉里"试试 -行
- Say "Larry" one more time. - Okay.

606
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:43,400
拉里
Larry.

607
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:52,060
你妈打电话跟你说要播我的电影啦
Your mother called you about the screening of my film.

608
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,540
她放我们鸽子了
She blew us off,

609
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:56,047
用被蜜蜂攻击了的烂理由
some lame excuse about being attacked by bees.

610
00:20:56,047 --> 00:20:57,531
管她的 我们开始看吧
Oh what the hell, let's start.

611
00:20:59,820 --> 00:21:01,240
你在那里干嘛
What are you doing over there?

612
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:03,120
你才在里面干嘛吧
What are you doing up there?

613
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,297
那是你跟前第一夫人小瓢虫·约翰逊吗
Is that you with Lady Bird Johnson?

614
00:21:05,297 --> 00:21:07,800
是啊 我可是当年衣柜杂志的
Sure is. I was Closet Magazine's

615
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,740
"业界不可错过新星"
"Movers and Groovers to Watch."

616
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,060
她做的介绍演说
She did the keynote,

617
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:12,560
还称赞了我的小胡子
complimented my mustache...

618
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:13,740
大好时光啊
Heady times.

619
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:15,360
那个新闻片段是怎么回事
What's with all that news footage?

620
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,688
历史背景也是很重要的
Well, historical context is important.

621
00:21:17,688 --> 00:21:18,753
政府水门事件丑闻过后
Post-Watergate,

622
00:21:18,753 --> 00:21:20,800
大众想要透明化
people wanted transparency,

623
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:21,740
所以设计了玻璃衣柜
hence the glass closet.

624
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:24,400
我跟你解释下为什么下一个镜头我没穿衣服
Now, let me explain why my shirt is off in the next shot.
